Apache-2.0 covers this repository and everything committed in it: the five
Python packages, and, as of 2026-08-30, the 72 model manifests, the 41
capability contracts, the 85 measurement records, and the evaluation inputs
under registry/evals/. Those inputs are computed rather than collected, with the
four qualifications recorded below.

Computed means ray-marched signed distance fields, additively synthesised audio,
analytic satellite bands, and document pages typeset from the very reference
text they will be scored against — no photograph and no recording of a person.
The four faces in registry/evals/bench/assets/visages-groupe.png do not exist
and never did; registry/evals/bench/README.md says why that was the only honest
way to build that load. The golden sets hold 79 committed data files — 44 inputs
under */assets/ and 35 references — and 71 of them come from one of the 44 cases
that carry a `source` block: every input, the 16 typeset reference texts a
document page is rendered from, and the 11 reference images computed in the same
pass as the input they are the ground truth of. tools/golden_assets.py rebuilds
55 of those 71 from the block alone; the 16 reference texts are the authority it
renders from, not its output. The 8 data files left over are the expected tool
calls under registry/evals/golden/tool-use/reference/, written here rather than
rendered. Of the 58 files under registry/evals/bench/assets/, 48 are rebuilt
either by that same script or, since 2026-08-24, by a recipe under tools/assets/
that tools/bench_assets.py drives. The twelve recordings the speech-to-text
golden set calls for do not exist:
registry/evals/golden/speech-to-text/SOURCING.md records that a public corpus was
deliberately not imported instead.

Where that is not the whole truth:

- Eight bench images have no committed recipe: assets/cube.png, sphere.png,
  cone.png, masque-cone.png, masque-fond.png, page-dense.png,
  page-paragraphe.png and page-tableau.png. They predate the rule that a load
  must say how it was made, and both tools/golden_assets.py and
  registry/evals/bench/README.md record that their recipe was never versioned.
  They are renders and not photographs — they carry no camera metadata, and they
  are what the README describes, three 256x256 RGBA solids on a genuinely
  transparent background, two 8-bit masks and three typeset pages — but that is
  this project's memory plus an inspection of the files, not a recipe anyone can
  re-run.
- assets/atelier-mouvement.mp4 records its parameters and the ffmpeg command
  that assembled it, but no committed script re-runs its `scene-animee` recipe.
- assets/parole-fr-32s.wav and assets/parole-tts.wav are not renders at all:
  they are output of a model in the parc, qwen3-tts-1.7b@8bit-mlx, which is
  itself Apache-2.0. The voice is synthetic and the spoken text was written
  here. The first has a committed recipe, tools/assets/parole.py; the second has
  only a note in registry/evals/bench/speaker-diarization.json.
- The three amino-acid sequences in registry/evals/bench/protein-embed.json —
  PDB entries 1UBQ, 2LYZ and 1GFL — are the one thing under registry/evals/ that
  was collected rather than computed. They come from the RCSB PDB under CC0 1.0
  per its usage policy, read against https://www.rcsb.org/fasta/entry/<code> on
  2026-08-24; that file's `provenance` field states this at length. CC0 requires
  no attribution, so this is not one — only a statement of where they came from.

The sixteen golden-set document pages are typeset with the macOS system fonts
that tools/golden_assets.py names: Times New Roman, Arial, Courier New. Their
rasterised glyphs are committed here; no font file is.

Apache-2.0 does not cover the model weights those manifests describe. Écurie
downloads them from their upstream hosts on `ecurie pull` and redistributes
none. Each weight keeps its own license, recorded in its manifest's `license`
and `license_class` fields as declared upstream, not as independently verified:
of the 72, thirteen are `restricted`, two are `research-only`, and two are
`unknown`. CAD-Recode is CC BY-NC 4.0 down to its inference code, which is why
that code is not committed here; MiniMax-H3 and Hunyuan3D 2.1 carry territorial
restrictions that reach the outputs they produce. Read the manifest before
running the model it describes.

packages/core, packages/store, packages/runtime, packages/api and packages/mcp
each hold a verbatim copy of LICENSE and of this file, so that the wheels and
sdists built from them carry both, as Section 4(a) of the License requires of
any redistribution. The copies at the root of the repository are the originals.
